  "title": "Consciousness evolved by natural selection, so it must affect behavior",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "88563788-4547-4d64-92c7-cdbe0a1f8084",
      "text": "The development of consciousness must be explainable through natural selection, and a property can be selected only if it affects behavior, so consciousness must have effects on behavior. Popper and Eccles press this against epiphenomenalism.",
